From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:23:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 131/144] GreatDANE: give URLManualDownload a query string so
 the stub suffix is valid (round 4h)

NGD 4f+4g MEDIUM: stub.nsh appends &installer_arch= to URLManualDownload. The
4f URL was https://dane.surf/download/ with no "?", which would produce a
broken path. It is now https://dane.surf/download/?channel=unofficial.

No stub installer is built: no Dane mozconfig sets MOZ_STUB_INSTALLER. The
branding.nsi comments say that plainly. stub.nsh itself is not edited (stock).

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
---
 browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi b/browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi
index 0cd1267c31..c7e1cc10b6 100644
--- a/browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi
+++ b/browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi
@@ -18,10 +18,14 @@
 # equivalent. The public Windows installer (2026-11-10) is the versioned
 # unsigned Dane-153.7.0esr-win64.installer.exe; pinning that filename would
 # rot, and the stub CertCheck cannot succeed until a signed build exists.
+# No stub installer is built: no Dane mozconfig sets MOZ_STUB_INSTALLER.
+# URLManualDownload includes ?channel=unofficial because stub.nsh appends
+# &installer_arch= to this URL when a stub is present; a bare path with no
+# "?" would produce a broken query.
 !define URLStubDownloadX86 "https://dane.surf/download/"
 !define URLStubDownloadAMD64 "https://dane.surf/download/"
 !define URLStubDownloadAArch64 "https://dane.surf/download/"
-!define URLManualDownload "https://dane.surf/download/"
+!define URLManualDownload "https://dane.surf/download/?channel=unofficial"
 !define URLSystemRequirements "https://dane.surf/support/"
 !define Channel "unofficial"
 
@@ -29,8 +33,11 @@
 # name used here (CertNameDownload subject CN and CertIssuerDownload issuer)
 # is the owner's decision before release. These placeholders are syntactically
 # valid NSIS string defines and must be replaced with the real identity before
-# any signed stub is shipped. Until then the stub's PE trust check is expected
-# to fail and fall back to URLManualDownload (the Dane download page).
+# any signed stub is shipped. No stub is built today (no mozconfig sets
+# MOZ_STUB_INSTALLER). If a stub is built later, its PE trust check is
+# expected to fail until a real identity is set, and URLManualDownload is
+# https://dane.surf/download/?channel=unofficial so the stub.nsh
+# &installer_arch= suffix is a valid query parameter.
 !define CertNameDownload   "TODO-NO-WINDOWS-SIGNING-IDENTITY-YET"
 !define CertIssuerDownload "TODO-NO-WINDOWS-SIGNING-IDENTITY-YET"
 
